dist/
*.exe
locals.txt

# Slate state. The DATABASE IS DERIVED and rebuildable from the patch chain,
# so it is not committed; `patches/` is the tracked record and must be.
db/
*.xlsx
*.xlsession

# One Claude Code session chunk per turn. Kept on disk and out of the repo:
# the database keeps the metadata, so a rebuild can still say which chunk it
# should have and when one is missing.
transcripts/

# Agent local overrides (machine-specific, must not be committed)
AGENTS.local.md

# Go workspace. Local cross-folder development only, and NEVER committed.
#
# It is what makes s55's maxim 2 affordable: `replace` in a go.mod travels
# with the repo and is forbidden, while a workspace is machine-local and is
# IGNORED by `go run module@sha`. The property that makes it irrelevant to an
# audit is exactly what makes it safe here. Committing one would reach every
# build from a checkout, including every test run.
go.work
go.work.sum
